  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "Functions of school",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\">Sociologists say school does several jobs:</p><ul><li><b>Teach subjects</b>.</li><li><b>Socialise</b> children into norms.</li><li><b>Prepare</b> for work.</li><li>Give equal chances.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "Hidden curriculum",
      "body_html": "<p>The <span class=\"hl p\">hidden curriculum</span> isn't on the timetable:</p><ul><li>Lining up.</li><li>Hands up to speak.</li><li>Wearing uniform.</li><li>Respecting authority.</li></ul><p>You learn these without anyone teaching them. 🤫</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "School and society",
      "body_html": "<p>School also helps society as a whole:</p><ul><li>Sorts people into roles.</li><li>Spreads shared values.</li><li>Builds the future workforce.</li></ul><p>Hence why UK school is compulsory from 5 to 18 (in some form). 📚</p>"
    }
  ],
